IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulation 1: Interpretation. Piece er1, layer 1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30
-- (../../registers/source-bundle/SOR-96-332.txt). Nothing here is verified against the official text. `src:N` is a line of that file.
-- Instrument: the Regulations, not the Act. The Act's own definitions are in the core (eia-core-interpretation).
--
-- Every rule takes plain facts as its own GIVEN (the stable binary rejects a GIVEN on a section) and is named
-- `reg N(M) <the Regulations' phrase>`. Types, constructors and fields begin `er1`.
-- A definition is a rule that says whether a thing is within the defined term; a fact about a person or a
-- family tree is a plain input the person can state. Where the definition points into the Act (subsections
-- 23.1(2), 23.2(3), 152.01(1) and the like), that provision is outside this piece and its result is an input.
--
-- No enactment, making or commencement date appears in lines 1 to 339 of the Regulations: the title block
-- (lines 5 to 7) and the enacting words (line 9) carry none, and the coming into force is Part VII (piece er6).
-- So this piece carries no commencement date and no rule takes a rule date.

§ `Regulation 1(1) - definitions`

-- The lead-in (line 12) and the definition of "Act" (line 13), which only names the Employment Insurance Act, are not encoded.

-- src:14 | pay period means the period in respect of which earnings are paid to or enjoyed by an insured person. (période de paie)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 1(1) "pay period" (src:14)
-- Plain gloss: the stretch of time that a payment of earnings is for. The insured person is the one the earnings
-- are paid to or enjoyed by (the core's `s 2(1) insured person` answers that).
GIVEN `the person is an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `earnings are paid to the person in respect of the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `earnings are enjoyed by the person in respect of the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 1(1) pay period` IF
        `the person is an insured person`
    AND (   `earnings are paid to the person in respect of the period`
         OR `earnings are enjoyed by the person in respect of the period`)

-- src:15 | self-employed person, other than in sections 30 and 35, has the same meaning as in subsection 152.01(1) of the Act. (travailleur indépendant)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 1(1) "self-employed person" (src:15)
-- Plain gloss: for the Regulations other than regs 30 and 35, "self-employed person" is the Act's word in
-- subsection 152.01(1), whose meaning is decided in piece ei5 (out of range: section 152.01 (piece ei5)).
-- In regs 30 and 35 the Regulations define the word for themselves (reg 30(5), piece er2; reg 35(1), piece er3),
-- so this definition says nothing there: NOTHING, an explicit "not decided here".
GIVEN `the word is used in section 30 or section 35 of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a self-employed person within the meaning of subsection 152.01(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 1(1) self-employed person, other than in sections 30 and 35` IS
    IF `the word is used in section 30 or section 35 of these Regulations`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the individual is a self-employed person within the meaning of subsection 152.01(1) of the Act`

§ `Regulation 1(2) - international organization`

-- src:16 | (2) For the purposes of these Regulations and section 5 of the Act, international organization means
-- src:17 | (a) any specialized agency of which Canada is a member that is brought into relationship with the United Nations in accordance with article 63 of the Charter of the United Nations; and
-- src:18 | (b) any international organization of which Canada is a member, the primary purpose of which is the maintenance of international peace or the economic or social well-being of a community of nations. (organisme international)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 1(2) "international organization" (src:16-18)
-- Plain gloss: either a United Nations specialized agency that Canada belongs to, or another organization that
-- Canada belongs to whose main purpose is world peace or the economic or social well-being of a group of nations.
-- The result is the fact that the core's `s 5(2)(e) employment by an international organization` takes as its
-- input `by an international organization`; the same definition governs reg 3(1) below.
GIVEN `the body is a specialized agency of which Canada is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is brought into relationship with the United Nations in accordance with article 63 of the Charter of the United Nations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is an international organization of which Canada is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its primary purpose is the maintenance of international peace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its primary purpose is the economic or social well-being of a community of nations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 1(2) international organization` IF
        (   `the body is a specialized agency of which Canada is a member`
        AND `it is brought into relationship with the United Nations in accordance with article 63 of the Charter of the United Nations`)
    OR  (   `the body is an international organization of which Canada is a member`
        AND (   `its primary purpose is the maintenance of international peace`
             OR `its primary purpose is the economic or social well-being of a community of nations`))

§ `Regulation 1(3) - family member`

-- The seventeen paragraphs (a) to (q) are independent kinds of relationship; a person may fall within several.
-- So the definition is a checkbox record with one BOOLEAN field per paragraph and a disjunction ("any one of
-- the following"), not an enum. Each field is worded as the paragraph states it, "the individual" being the
-- person the question is asked about. Paragraph (q) is an open standard and is taken as the individual (or the
-- other person) states it. Paragraphs (o) and (p) use the words "ward" and "guardian", which reg 1(4) defines
-- below; their fields are the facts those two rules decide (a seat layer feeds them from `reg 1(4) ward` and
-- `reg 1(4) guardian`). The Act's subsections that this definition serves (23.1(2), 23.2(1), 23.3(1), 152.06(1),
-- 152.061(1), 152.062(1)) are outside this piece: whether a relationship is "described" there is their question.
-- src:19 | (3) The following definitions apply in these Regulations and in subsections 23.1(2), 23.2(1), 23.3(1), 152.06(1), 152.061(1) and 152.062(1) of the Act.
-- src:20 | family member, in relation to an individual, means any one of the following:
-- src:21 | (a) the spouse or common-law partner of the individual;
-- src:22 | (b) a child of the individual or a child of the individual’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:23 | (c) a parent of the individual or a spouse or common-law partner of the parent;
-- src:24 | (d) a child of the individual’s parent or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the individual’s parent;
-- src:25 | (e) a grandparent of the individual or of the individual’s spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual’s grandparent;
-- src:26 | (f) a grandchild of the individual or of the individual’s spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual’s grandchild;
-- src:27 | (g) the spouse or common-law partner of the individual’s child or of the child of the individual’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:28 | (h) a parent, or the spouse or common-law partner of a parent, of the individual’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:29 | (i) the spouse or common-law partner of a child of the individual’s parent or of a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the individual’s parent;
-- src:30 | (j) a child of a parent of the individual’s spouse or common-law partner or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the parent of the individual’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:31 | (k) an uncle or aunt of the individual or of the individual’s spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual’s uncle or aunt;
-- src:32 | (l) a nephew or niece of the individual or of the individual’s spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual’s nephew or niece;
-- src:33 | (m) a current or former foster parent of the individual or of the individual’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:34 | (n) a current or former foster child of the individual or the spouse or common-law partner of that child;
-- src:35 | (o) a current or former ward of the individual or of the individual’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:36 | (p) a current or former guardian of the individual or the spouse or common-law partner of that guardian;
-- src:37 | (q) a person, whether or not related to the individual by marriage, common-law partnership, or any legal parent-child relationship, whom the individual considers to be like a close relative or who considers the individual to be like a close relative. (membre de la famille)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 1(3) "family member" (src:19-37)
DECLARE `er1 Relationship to an individual` HAS
    `er1 (a) the spouse or common-law partner of the individual`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (b) a child of the individual or a child of the individual's spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (c) a parent of the individual or a spouse or common-law partner of the parent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (d) a child of the individual's parent or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's parent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (e) a grandparent of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's grandparent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (f) a grandchild of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's grandchild` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (g) the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's child or of the child of the individual's spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (h) a parent, or the spouse or common-law partner of a parent, of the individual's spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (i) the spouse or common-law partner of a child of the individual's parent or of a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's parent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (j) a child of a parent of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the parent of the individual's spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (k) an uncle or aunt of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's uncle or aunt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (l) a nephew or niece of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's nephew or niece` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (m) a current or former foster parent of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (n) a current or former foster child of the individual or the spouse or common-law partner of that child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (o) a current or former ward of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (p) a current or former guardian of the individual or the spouse or common-law partner of that guardian` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er1 (q) a person whom the individual considers to be like a close relative or who considers the individual to be like a close relative` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 1(3) "family member" (src:20-37)
-- Plain gloss: a relative by blood, marriage, common-law partnership or legal parent-child relationship out to
-- uncles, aunts, nephews, nieces and grandchildren, a foster, ward or guardian relationship, or anyone treated as
-- like a close relative. Paragraph (q) holds "whether or not related ... by marriage, common-law partnership, or any
-- legal parent-child relationship", so it needs no family tie.
GIVEN relationship IS A `er1 Relationship to an individual`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 1(3) family member` IF
       relationship's `er1 (a) the spouse or common-law partner of the individual`
    OR relationship's `er1 (b) a child of the individual or a child of the individual's spouse or common-law partner`
    OR relationship's `er1 (c) a parent of the individual or a spouse or common-law partner of the parent`
    OR relationship's `er1 (d) a child of the individual's parent or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's parent`
    OR relationship's `er1 (e) a grandparent of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's grandparent`
    OR relationship's `er1 (f) a grandchild of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's grandchild`
    OR relationship's `er1 (g) the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's child or of the child of the individual's spouse or common-law partner`
    OR relationship's `er1 (h) a parent, or the spouse or common-law partner of a parent, of the individual's spouse or common-law partner`
    OR relationship's `er1 (i) the spouse or common-law partner of a child of the individual's parent or of a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's parent`
    OR relationship's `er1 (j) a child of a parent of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the parent of the individual's spouse or common-law partner`
    OR relationship's `er1 (k) an uncle or aunt of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's uncle or aunt`
    OR relationship's `er1 (l) a nephew or niece of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner or the spouse or common-law partner of the individual's nephew or niece`
    OR relationship's `er1 (m) a current or former foster parent of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner`
    OR relationship's `er1 (n) a current or former foster child of the individual or the spouse or common-law partner of that child`
    OR relationship's `er1 (o) a current or former ward of the individual or of the individual's spouse or common-law partner`
    OR relationship's `er1 (p) a current or former guardian of the individual or the spouse or common-law partner of that guardian`
    OR relationship's `er1 (q) a person whom the individual considers to be like a close relative or who considers the individual to be like a close relative`

-- src:38 | nurse practitioner means a registered nurse who, under the laws of a province, is entitled to practise as a nurse practitioner — or under an equivalent designation — and to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients. (infirmier praticien)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 1(3) "nurse practitioner" (src:38)
-- Plain gloss: a registered nurse whom a province's laws let practise as a nurse practitioner (or under an
-- equivalent title) and make diagnoses on their own, order and read tests, prescribe and treat. All six are required.
GIVEN `a registered nurse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entitled under the laws of a province to practise as a nurse practitioner or under an equivalent designation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entitled to autonomously make diagnoses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entitled to autonomously order and interpret diagnostic tests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entitled to autonomously prescribe substances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entitled to autonomously treat patients` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 1(3) nurse practitioner` IF
        `a registered nurse`
    AND `entitled under the laws of a province to practise as a nurse practitioner or under an equivalent designation`
    AND `entitled to autonomously make diagnoses`
    AND `entitled to autonomously order and interpret diagnostic tests`
    AND `entitled to autonomously prescribe substances`
    AND `entitled to autonomously treat patients`

§ `Regulation 1(4) - guardian and ward`

-- src:39 | (4) For the purpose of the definition family member in subsection (3), guardian means a person who is legally authorized to act on behalf of a minor or incapable adult and includes a tutor, curator, mandatary acting under a protection mandate or any person who is appointed to act in a similar capacity and ward means a person for whom a guardian is appointed.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 1(4) "guardian" (src:39)
-- Plain gloss: someone the law authorizes to act for a child or for an adult who cannot manage for themselves.
-- "includes" adds the four named kinds (tutor, curator, mandatary under a protection mandate, any person appointed
-- in a similar capacity) to the general words; each counts whether or not the general words are also met.
-- Applies "for the purpose of the definition family member in subsection (3)" only.
GIVEN `legally authorized to act on behalf of a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `legally authorized to act on behalf of an incapable adult` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a tutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a curator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a mandatary acting under a protection mandate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person appointed to act in a similar capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 1(4) guardian` IF
       `legally authorized to act on behalf of a minor`
    OR `legally authorized to act on behalf of an incapable adult`
    OR `a tutor`
    OR `a curator`
    OR `a mandatary acting under a protection mandate`
    OR `a person appointed to act in a similar capacity`

-- src:39 | (4) For the purpose of the definition family member in subsection (3), guardian means a person who is legally authorized to act on behalf of a minor or incapable adult and includes a tutor, curator, mandatary acting under a protection mandate or any person who is appointed to act in a similar capacity and ward means a person for whom a guardian is appointed.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 1(4) "ward" (src:39)
-- Plain gloss: the person a guardian has been appointed for.
GIVEN `a guardian is appointed for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 1(4) ward` IF
    `a guardian is appointed for the person`

§ `Regulation 1(5) - care and support`

-- Both definitions serve paragraphs 23.1(2)(b), 23.2(1)(a), 23.3(1)(a), 152.06(1)(b), 152.061(1)(a) and 152.062(1)(a)
-- of the Act (out of range: pieces ei1 and ei5). "A family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the
-- Act, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult" is one BOOLEAN input: those provisions, and reg 1(6) and (7)
-- below, decide it.
-- src:40 | (5) The following definitions apply in these Regulations and in paragraphs 23.‍1(2)‍(b), 23.‍2(1)‍(a), 23.‍3(1)‍(a), 152.‍06(1)‍(b), 152.‍061(1)‍(a) and 152.‍062(1)‍(a) of the Act.
-- src:41 | care means all care that is required because of the state of health of a family member referred to in subsections 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult, other than the care provided by a health care professional. (soins)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 1(5) "care" (src:40-41)
-- Plain gloss: the hands-on help the sick person needs, other than what a health care professional provides.
GIVEN `the person needing it is a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is required because of the state of health of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is provided by a health care professional` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 1(5) care` IF
        `the person needing it is a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult`
    AND `it is required because of the state of health of that person`
    AND NOT (`it is provided by a health care professional`)

-- src:40 | (5) The following definitions apply in these Regulations and in paragraphs 23.‍1(2)‍(b), 23.‍2(1)‍(a), 23.‍3(1)‍(a), 152.‍06(1)‍(b), 152.‍061(1)‍(a) and 152.‍062(1)‍(a) of the Act.
-- src:42 | support means all psychological or emotional support that is required because of the state of health of a family member referred to in subsections 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult. (soutien)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 1(5) "support" (src:42)
-- Plain gloss: the psychological or emotional support the sick person needs. Unlike "care", the definition has no
-- exception for a health care professional.
GIVEN `the person needing it is a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is required because of the state of health of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 1(5) support` IF
        `the person needing it is a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult`
    AND `it is required because of the state of health of that person`

§ `Regulation 1(6) and (7) - critically ill child and critically ill adult`

-- The age tests are made on "the day on which the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) [or
-- 23.3(3) or 152.062(3)] of the Act begins" (that day is outside this piece: pieces ei1 and ei5). A person is 18
-- on their eighteenth birthday and not before: `add years` of the date of birth by 18 is that birthday (it
-- clamps 29 February to 28 February in a year that has no 29 February; the Regulations do not say which day a
-- person born on 29 February reaches 18, see NOTES.md fork register).
-- src:44 | critically ill child means a person who is under 18 years of age on the day on which the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) of the Act begins, whose baseline state of health has significantly changed and whose life is at risk as a result of an illness or injury. (enfant gravement malade)
-- src:46 | critically ill adult means a person who is 18 years of age or older on the day on which the period referred to in subsection 23.3(3) or 152.062(3) of the Act begins, whose baseline state of health has significantly changed and whose life is at risk as a result of an illness or injury. (adulte gravement malade)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 1(6) and (7) (src:44) (src:46)
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 1(6) and (7) the person has reached the age of 18 on the day` IF
    `the day on which the period begins` AT LEAST `add years` `date of birth` 18

-- src:43 | (6) The following definition applies in these Regulations and in subsection 23.2(1) and 152.061(1) of the Act.
-- src:44 | critically ill child means a person who is under 18 years of age on the day on which the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) of the Act begins, whose baseline state of health has significantly changed and whose life is at risk as a result of an illness or injury. (enfant gravement malade)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 1(6) "critically ill child" (src:43-44)
-- Plain gloss: a child under 18 whose usual state of health has changed a lot and whose life is at risk because of
-- an illness or injury.
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) of the Act begins` IS A DATE
      `baseline state of health has significantly changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `life is at risk as a result of an illness or injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 1(6) critically ill child` IF
        NOT (`reg 1(6) and (7) the person has reached the age of 18 on the day` `date of birth` `the day on which the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) of the Act begins`)
    AND `baseline state of health has significantly changed`
    AND `life is at risk as a result of an illness or injury`

-- src:45 | (7) The following definition applies in these Regulations and in subsections 23.3(1) and 152.062(1) of the Act.
-- src:46 | critically ill adult means a person who is 18 years of age or older on the day on which the period referred to in subsection 23.3(3) or 152.062(3) of the Act begins, whose baseline state of health has significantly changed and whose life is at risk as a result of an illness or injury. (adulte gravement malade)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 1(7) "critically ill adult" (src:45-46)
-- Plain gloss: a person of 18 or older whose usual state of health has changed a lot and whose life is at risk
-- because of an illness or injury.
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period referred to in subsection 23.3(3) or 152.062(3) of the Act begins` IS A DATE
      `baseline state of health has significantly changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `life is at risk as a result of an illness or injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 1(7) critically ill adult` IF
        `reg 1(6) and (7) the person has reached the age of 18 on the day` `date of birth` `the day on which the period referred to in subsection 23.3(3) or 152.062(3) of the Act begins`
    AND `baseline state of health has significantly changed`
    AND `life is at risk as a result of an illness or injury`
